.TH MU2EDAQ-COMMANDLINE-TOOLS-START 1 "2026-07-27" "mu2edaq-commandline-tools 0.2.0" "Mu2e DAQ"
.SH NAME
start-mu2edaq-commandline-tools.sh \- refresh the venv and run mu2edaq-tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./start-mu2edaq-commandline-tools.sh
.RI [ \-\-no\-update ]
.RI [ tool-arguments ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bootstraps the virtual environment on first run, refreshes dependencies on
later runs, writes its pid to a pidfile, and then execs the
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1)
dispatcher. Every argument after the options below is passed straight through,
so
.PP
.RS
.nf
./start\-mu2edaq\-commandline\-tools.sh config \-\-json
.fi
.RE
.PP
is
.B mu2edaq-tools config --json
run inside the venv, with no activation needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-no\-update
Skip the dependency refresh and start immediately. Use on nodes without
network access, or when you know the venv is current.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit. Only recognised as the first argument; afterwards
.B \-h
belongs to the tool being run.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_TOOLS_PIDFILE
Pidfile location. Default:
.IR .mu2edaq-tools.pid " in the checkout."
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the dispatched tool.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2edaq-tools (1),
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-stop (1),
.BR mu2edaq-commandline-tools-bootstrap (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ group.
